{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbcqmfkyhiLxTtZNQZBz", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Flags in this project are simple, file-based on/off switches.\n\n**How they work**\n- They're declared in `flags.toml` at the repo root, under the `[flags]` table. Right now there's one:\n  ```toml\n  [flags]\n  invoice-pdf-v2 = false\n  ```\n- You read them only through `flags.is_on(\"name\")` from `src/flags.py`. There's also `flags.all_flags()`, which returns all of them as a dict.\n- Flag names use kebab-case.\n\n**For your checkout flow**\n1. Declare the flag in `flags.toml`:\n   ```toml\n   [flags]\n   invoice-pdf-v2 = false\n   checkout-v2 = false\n   ```\n2. Check it where the flow branches:\n   ```python\n   from src import flags\n\n   if flags.is_on(\"checkout-v2\"):\n       return new_checkout(...)\n   return legacy_checkout(...)\n   ```\n\n**Things to watch for** (from `src/flags.py`)\n- **Typos fail silently.** `is_on()` uses `_FLAGS.get(name, False)`, so a misspelled or undeclared name returns `False` with no error. You'll just stay on the old flow without knowing why. Copy the name exactly from `flags.toml`.\n- **Changes need a restart.** `flags.toml` is read once, when the module is imported. Editing it won't affect a process that's already running.\n- **There are no per-user or percentage rollouts.** A flag is a single global true/false for the whole deployment. For a gradual rollout of checkout you'd need to build that yourself.\n\nI can add the flag and wire up the branch point if you tell me where the checkout entry point is."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 421, "cache_read_input_tokens": 25415, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 421}, "output_tokens": 3, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "023099a3-b5ef-41f9-83b0-9bc0e438e5a8", "uuid": "ef6a945c-4e52-4e5e-8aa5-18a35277a5a4", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T13:45:44.052Z", "request_id": "req_011CfbcqmMuoPaTgsnH2LU8S"}
